// The riders' horse line: the steal route for the ford.
@speaker The horse line
=== start
[flag ford_settled] -> settled
[flag horses_watched] -> watched
[night] -> dark
Twenty horses on a picket line, small and shaggy and better fed than anyone in Vindomagos. Two riders sit on a log where they can see the whole line, and they're watching you now.

Not in daylight.
* Find a place in the reeds and wait for dark. -> wait ~ wait_until 22
* Leave them. -> END

=== wait
The light goes. The fire across the camp burns down to red, and the men around it go quiet one by one. There's one guard left on the log, wrapped to the eyes in his cloak.
-> choose

=== dark
The horses shift and blow in the dark. One guard on the log, wrapped in his cloak.
-> choose

=== choose
* [roll sneak 0] Cut the picket rope and drive them off into the night. -> stolen | caught
* [survival 50] Lead them off quietly, a few at a time, the way you'd move cattle. -> stolen_quiet
* Leave them. -> END

=== stolen
~ set horses_gone; quest ford horses_stolen; xp 100
The rope parts under your knife. You slap the nearest rump, and the whole line goes, a drumming in the dark that wakes everyone at once. By the time the riders are on their feet, cursing in their own language, the horses are halfway to the hills.

Now they're men on foot.
* Slip away. -> END

=== stolen_quiet
~ set horses_gone; set horses_kept; quest ford horses_stolen; xp 125
You take them three and four at a time, a hand on each neck, up the valley to a fold in the hills above the old sheepfold where nobody will find them before morning. It takes half the night. The guard on the log never wakes.

Twenty horses is a fortune. It is also, now, something to bargain with.
* Slip away. -> END

=== caught
The guard isn't as asleep as he looked. He shouts, and all over the camp men are throwing off their cloaks and reaching for spears.
* [roll AGI 0] Drop into the reeds and run. -> fled | cornered
* [roll speech -10] Stand still with your hands open. "Easy. Easy. I came looking for Haldo." -> bluffed | cornered
* Fight. -> fight

=== fled
~ set horses_watched
You're in the reeds before the spears get there, running bent double with the river to your knees, and then lying flat in the mud while they beat the bank above you with spear shafts and swear in their own language. After a long time they give up and go back to the fire.

From now on there will be more than one man on that log.
* Crawl away. -> END

=== bluffed
~ set horses_watched
They walk you to the fire with a spear at your back. Haldo sits up in his blankets and looks at you for a long time.

"Looking for me," he says. "In my horses. In the dark." Then he laughs, and some of the others laugh because he did. "Come in daylight next time, farmer, like a man with business. Now go away before I change my mind."
* Go, while he's laughing. -> END

=== cornered
They're around you before you've gone ten paces, a ring of spear points and angry faces in the firelight. Haldo pushes through, barefoot, with his spear.

"Horse thief," he says. "Give me a reason not to."
* [silver 20] Hold out twenty silver. "For your trouble. And my life." -> paid ~ silver -20
* [roll PRE -10] Look at him and say nothing at all. -> stared | fight
* Fight. -> fight

=== paid
~ set horses_watched
He takes it, weighs it, and nods at the dark. "Your life is cheap. Go."
* Go. -> END

=== stared
~ set horses_watched
The silence stretches. Somebody coughs. Haldo looks away first, and covers it by spitting in the fire. "Not worth the digging," he says. "Get out of my camp."
* Go. -> END

=== fight
~ set ford_fought; fight_all riders
Five of them, and the river at your back.
* Fight. -> END

=== watched
Three riders sit on the log by the picket line now, awake, with their spears across their knees. One of them sees you and lifts his spear an inch, and smiles.
* Leave them. -> END

=== settled
The picket line is quiet. The horses are none of your business now.
* Leave them. -> END
